 "policy": "Reviewed links from a company named in an official document to a U.S.-listed ticker: sponsor or named entity -> legal entity -> listed company (itself or its parent) -> ticker -> evidence. A row is added only for the listed company itself, a division of it, a wholly owned subsidiary, or a renamed company; joint ventures, partly owned, private and non-U.S.-listed companies go to 'excluded' with the reason. Matching is exact on the normalised name (case, punctuation and a trailing legal suffix such as Inc/LLC/Corp removed); there is no similarity matching. Each row's evidence page is fetched on a runner and checked for the listed text before the row is marked verified. A row is used only after its evidence check passed on a runner (evidence_verified_run); a row without it is listed as EVIDENCE_PENDING and not linked. Ownership changes over time: a row may carry valid_from/valid_to (YYYY-MM-DD) with validity_source, and links only documents dated inside that window (OUTSIDE_RELATION_VALIDITY otherwise); a name may have several rows for different windows. A parent named in a document is not linked to a listed subsidiary (PARENT_OF_LISTED_COMPANY). 'names' holds the legal name and other reviewed names (trade, short or former names); each link records which one matched (name_basis). scripts/build_federal_register_feed.py validate_links() checks every row.",
